# The `agent-gateway-db-mode` group, lifted VERBATIM out of prometheusrule.yaml (comments
# stripped — the manifest is their one home) — the rules file db-mode.promtool-test loads.
# Not a manifest: `promtool test rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`). Named
# .promtool-rules rather than .yaml because manifest-lint kubeconforms every *.yaml under
# argocd/resources.
#
# DRIFT-PINNED by prometheus-rules-lint (expr + for per alert name, both directions). RE-COPY AFTER
# EVERY EXPR EDIT, then re-attach this header:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups":[{"name":"agent-gateway-db-mode","rules":[.spec.groups[] | select(.name == "agent-gateway-db-mode") | .rules[]]}]}' argocd/resources/agent-gateway/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
groups:
  - name: agent-gateway-db-mode
    rules:
      - alert: GatewayStoreMemoryMode
        expr: |
          max(gateway_db_mode{job="agent-gateway",mode="memory"}) == 1
        for: 5m
        labels:
          severity: warning
          triage: now
        annotations:
          summary: 'The gateway runs on its fail-open memory store — sessions, caps and rotated credentials do not survive its next restart'
          description: 'gateway_db_mode{mode="memory"} is 1: the gateway did not open its PVC store at start, so it admits rides from memory and forgets them at the next restart. Check: (1) kubectl -n agent-egress logs deploy/agent-gateway | grep "db: memory" names the path and the error (missing, read-only or corrupt); (2) GET /healthz on the gateway answers db: memory; (3) the agent-gateway Deployment mounts its /data PVC. The contract is gateway/specs/endpoints/health.md (GW-HEALTH) and gateway/specs/endpoints/metrics.md (GW-METRICS).'
